/P 525 0 R
/E (The leftover core becomes a neutron star: about 20 kilometers across, yet more massive than the Sun. A teaspoon of neutron star material would weigh billions of tons. These objects spin rapidly, sometimes emitting beams of radiation like cosmic lighthouses. Dense, extreme, and slightly terrifying.   )
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [13 14]
>>
